{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/320882-let-s-discuss-ldi-a-second-need-some-ideas","id":320882,"title":"Let's discuss LDI a second ...need some ideas...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-24T10:53:40-08:00","id":320882,"title":"Let's discuss LDI a second ...need some ideas...","content":"So Last Dynasty International...my premise:<br /> <br /> Steals a vessel from PC Mummy. Specifically to lure the mummy out and capture it for their pharma purposes.<br /> <br /> They have a security capture team, specialists to make this happen...<br /> <br /> What would that look like given the powers of the Arisen. What equipment, supernaturals, what books in the current nWOD would help build that team?<br /> <br /> What tactics? Powers...etc...<br /> <br /> What do you think an LDI capture team would look like?<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4371-mfrantz2361","name":"mfrantz2361","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T12:27:01-08:00","id":320997,"title":"","content":"In my game, I mostly treat the LDI acquisition teams like a team of elite soldiers. I gave a few flare guns for use as particularly nasty weapons in an emergency (I don't imagine LDI wants Mummies to be suffering too much Aggravated Damage, since it makes death while extracting Sekhem much more likely, so I decided against incendiary rounds as the default). The big one was that I decided that one drug LDI produced rendered those who took it Witnesses. Pretty much vital for any group of mortals planning on taking on a Mummy. Terror Sybaris would render any attempt to bring a Mummy in alive useless.<br /> <br /> For supernatural support, I just assume they have access to a variety of Greater Amkhata. Jackal-headed for tracking, Falcon-headed for guarding, and either a Lion-headed Bull or Snake if they know the Mummy's location and just want to overwhelm it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T12:53:44-08:00","id":321003,"title":"","content":"No strike team. LDI stays in business by being smart. Taking on a mummy at the peak of its power with brute force isn't smart, it's suicide.<br /> <br /> Instead, LDI uses best occult researchers, historians and strategists you can hire to figure out weaknesses of the mummy in question - extensive histories. Psychological profiles. With memory being fleeting and all, LDI knows more about the mummy than she does about herself.<br /> <br /> They have inserted moles in the mummy's cult. A mummy's memory and sense of identity is maintained, in its first couple days, by its cult, yes? If LDI controls the cult, it, by extension, also controls the mummy.<br /> <br /> The idea is to use an approach, any approach, that cannot easily be countered by a mummy boosting her strength to 10 and going on a rampage. LDI doesn't maintain its success by fighting battles it can't win, or where winning isn't really worth the effort from a cost-benefit point of view. Narratively, they don't fill the role of an antagonist that can easily be defeated by physical means. That's what the Amkhata or even some Shuankhsen are there for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T12:55:48-08:00","id":321004,"title":"","content":"Ok I think I'm with you there. I'm on the right track. Using your witness requirement: Something like 6 to 8 men with USAS combat shotguns (Lots of Bashing damage), 2 of them with some kind of high tension wire netguns...Greater Amkhata in support...I was thinking of some kind of instant hardening foam spray to at least slow down the Mummy. But how do you deal with capturing a Mummy with Obedient Clay? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4371-mfrantz2361","name":"mfrantz2361","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T12:58:48-08:00","id":321006,"title":"","content":"Dust Beneath Feet poses an even bigger challenge (&quot;You've got me surrounded? I dunno, I'm standing on metal/dirt/concrete/any conceivable ground that isn't wood or plastic&quot;). Sometimes, having a winged snake-bodied Amkhat materialise on top of them at the start of the fight might be the only way to get anything like good odds for a successful retrieval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:01:13-08:00","id":321008,"title":"","content":"Good stuff Christian thank you also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4371-mfrantz2361","name":"mfrantz2361","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:03:32-08:00","id":321010,"title":"","content":"the only problem with this idea of LDI is that in order for them to stay in business, how many Arisen do you think they've captured and utilized? It seems they get a lot of doses ...but if they had any methodology to keep up their business they would have to have a steady supply of Arisen...they must be good at keeping that business flowing or they would be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4371-mfrantz2361","name":"mfrantz2361","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T14:37:13-08:00","id":321057,"title":"","content":"I agree with that, mfrantz. And it's why I partly disagree with Christian A. That kind of approach is excellent, and I'm sure LDI has dedicated teams working at it. Sometimes though, brute force has its advantages. Obviously not when the Mummy is Sekhem 10, but using violence to seize a Mummy is a widely applicable tactic that doesn't require the specialised and lengthy research/mole system. So long as it can be done quietly and without collateral, it can quite easily be justified in the company balance sheet.<br /> <br /> Once a Mummy's Khat, and ideally canopic jars, have been seized, the company has the ability to summon said Mummy so long as they can identify the appropriate procedure and obtain a relic/vestige to sacrifice. I imagine this is where most of their Sekhem comes from, through summoning the Mummy under very carefully controlled conditions, letting their Sekhem run down a bit until they are no longer a threat, and then &quot;milking&quot; them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T21:41:06-08:00","id":321409,"title":"","content":"All very good points. I have an LDI team in training as we discuss this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We'll see how they do soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4371-mfrantz2361","name":"mfrantz2361","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T21:48:20-08:00","id":321414,"title":"","content":"My favourite little detail from the core on how LDI operates was the section on Integrated Transport Solutions (or something along those lines). Namely, the example when it talks about ordering, manufacturing, and transporting enough poison to poison an entire Mummy's cult. All through using a series of gormless employees with absolutely no knowledge as to what they're doing.<br /> <br /> It's not a nice thing to spring on a player, by any means, but it seems like LDI can employ a beautiful combination of &quot;shock and awe&quot;, blitzkrieg-esque overwhelming force against a target, that is simultaneously low-key, hard to trace, and strikes from an unexpected angle (poison in the cultist's water supply or something). It's a great concept, but thus far I've had a hard time of thinking of a way to employ such tactics in my own game that don't also just remove players from the game without a chance of avoiding it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:16:48-08:00","id":322342,"title":"","content":"When it comes to fighting mummies head on, I imagine they use weapons like out of the future weapons from armory reloaded: dazzlers to blind, screamers to deafen, shock weapons to stun them (unless I forgot something that would indicate that mummies aren't stunned by electrocution), maybe tranq rounds with alchemically enhanced ammunition, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if your strength 50 if you can't see, can't hear, can't move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:42:24-08:00","id":322368,"title":"","content":"I'm less sure about future weaponry. They're a pharmaceutical company with branches in animal conservation and an occult research department. When I give LDI advanced technology, I prefer to make it medical in nature (the Sekhem-imbued blood coagulator thing from the core is a great example) or related to Sekhem detection in some way.<br /> <br /> Of course, they're an obscenely wealthy company, so they do have access to the best weapons money can buy. Just not the cutting edge stuff that isn't on the market yet.<br /> <br /> The general principle though is certainly a good idea. I must remember that the next time my players go up against an LDI acquisitions team. More debilitating stuff (flash bangs, nets, and so on) and less direct damage weaponry. As for electricity, I thought I read somewhere that Mummies aren't stunned by electricity but are damaged by it, but I have no clue where I could have read that. One my main gripes about the core book was that it never clearly established what being undead actually meant in terms of being a Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T20:27:46-08:00","id":323366,"title":"","content":"Dantius Ganuducci IV would probably sell LDI the stuff I mentioned at a discount in return for detailed reports on how well the stuff worked on mummies, so I wouldn't exactly consider it going whole hog against the players.<br /> <br /> Now LDI killing cultists to reanimate them as undead cyborgs ala Antagonists or sending in rats with human brain tissue ala skinchangers now that would be going too far, even though I could see the study of sekhem leading to reanimation technology and chimerization. It just wouldn't have the right tone for mummy I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T01:36:04-08:00","id":323522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/320882-let-s-discuss-ldi-a-second-need-some-ideas?p=323366#post323366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now LDI killing cultists to reanimate them as undead cyborgs ala Antagonists or sending in rats with human brain tissue ala skinchangers now that would be going too far, even though I could see the study of sekhem leading to reanimation technology and chimerization. It just wouldn't have the right tone for mummy I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a lot of overlap between LDI and Cheiron<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:34:43-08:00","id":323622,"title":"","content":"Yes, but LDI has enough specialized (read: obscure) knowledge about the Arisen to have been able to corner a niche on that market. I suspect they're a thorn in Cheiron's side even though their board members totally play golf together.<br /> <br /> Yes I am aware of the strangeness of Cheiron's board. I take nothing back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T21:17:48-08:00","id":325042,"title":"","content":"Yes, I could see LDI and Cheiron going lots of ways- deadly enemies, friendly rivals, or partnership. <br /> <br /> I don't think draining a mummy would make them less attractive as spare parts for Cheiron, and well if LDI ships the mummies to Cheiron for disposal- either the mummy will be splitting its vengeance between two targets, or just go after Cheiron, so it would be win win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T22:00:57-08:00","id":325076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/320882-let-s-discuss-ldi-a-second-need-some-ideas?p=325042#post325042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, I could see LDI and Cheiron going lots of ways- deadly enemies, friendly rivals, or partnership.<br /> <br /> I don't think draining a mummy would make them less attractive as spare parts for Cheiron, and well if LDI ships the mummies to Cheiron for disposal- either the mummy will be splitting its vengeance between two targets, or just go after Cheiron, so it would be win win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I was thinking that LDI would be guarding the secrets of Sekhem with their bodyguards and lawyers but looking at it more closely, I start to realize there is a bit of a difference in market utilization. <br /> <br /> Cheiron's bread and butter is going after the supernatural creatures by volume. Werewolves, Kindred, Changelings, etc. Anything they can get goes on the slab for R&amp;D. Given this mandate, they simply can't afford to have the specialized facilities designed to go after the Arisen.<br /> <br /> Sure, they've managed to capture a few that were at their weakest and chop them up but after the board saw what happened to the Cell that got implanted with those organs... They decide the cost to benefit analysis was too high to focus on such a niche creature when you can focus on other ones that are both containable and active.<br /> <br /> LDI by contrast does have the facilities up and running to handle Arisen and does go directly after them which makes things interesting.<br /> <br /> Now that you mention it, I can see an LDI exec going on about the benefits of Sekhem with the Cheiron one replying &quot;But we can do the same thing by draining those vampires dry.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T20:05:28-08:00","id":326563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/320882-let-s-discuss-ldi-a-second-need-some-ideas?p=323522#post323522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite a lot of overlap between LDI and Cheiron</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A successful business model invites competitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}